+# Feature Specification: JSON Patch
+
+**Feature Branch**: `002-json-patch`
+**Input**: "Implement JSON Patch (RFC 6902): export `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`."
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `applyPatch(document, patch)` MUST be exported from `src/index.ts` and return the patched document as a new value.
+- **FR-002**: Neither `document` nor `patch` MUST be modified, and the result MUST NOT share structure with them. A failing patch has no effect (atomic).
+- **FR-003**: A patch MUST be an array of objects with string `op` and `path` (a JSON Pointer, RFC 6901); unknown ops, missing/mistyped members and invalid pointers MUST throw. Extra members are ignored.
+- **FR-004**: `add`: sets/inserts at the path (array index `0..length`, `-` appends; replaces an existing member; path `""` replaces the document). The parent MUST exist. `value` is required.
+- **FR-005**: `remove`: target MUST exist. Removing the root throws (no JSON document would remain).
+- **FR-006**: `replace`: target MUST exist; `value` required.
+- **FR-007**: `move`: remove `from` then add at `path`; `from` MUST exist; moving a location into its own child throws; same location is a no-op.
+- **FR-008**: `copy`: add a deep copy of the value at `from` to `path`.
+- **FR-009**: `test`: throws unless the target equals `value` (JSON equality: object member order irrelevant, array order significant, types strict).
+- **FR-010**: Only own members are addressable (`/constructor`, `/__proto__` inherited); an added `__proto__` member is plain data.
+
+## Success Criteria
+- All RFC 6902 Appendix A examples produce the documented results (or errors).
